cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software in research, please cite the specific archived version you
  pinned, not the repository in general. Each release has its own version DOI; see the
  "Archived releases" table in README.md.
title: research-core
abstract: >-
  Shared substrate for the scala-tessella research programme on tilings: exact rational
  and cyclotomic arithmetic, the Delaney-Dress symbol engine, the exact angle/moduli
  layer, exported algebraic rank witnesses, the U(z) class machinery, and a SAT/DRAT
  certification harness. No theorems live here; individual results live in their own
  verification repositories and depend on a pinned release.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mario
    family-names: Càllisto
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1215-3278
    email: mario.callisto@gmail.com
    alias: mcallisto
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/scala-tessella/research-core
url: https://github.com/scala-tessella/research-core
# The latest ARCHIVED release, which is what a citation must resolve to. Archiving follows the publication of
# a GitHub release, not the tag that publishes to Maven Central, so most versions on Central have no Zenodo
# deposit and nothing citable names them (0.3.0, 0.4.0, 0.6.x, 0.7.x and 0.8.0 among them); this block moves
# forward only when a release is archived and its version DOI is minted, which is necessarily the commit after
# the archived tag.
version: 0.8.1
date-released: '2026-09-01'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22238457
keywords:
  - tilings
  - tessellations
  - Delaney-Dress symbols
  - exact arithmetic
  - formal verification
  - Scala
